WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:03.440
[Narrator:] Every town. The town in which
you and I live. In the North, South, East, or West.

00:01:03.579 --> 00:01:09.479
Our homes. Our work. Our recreations make
Everytown what it is. 

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:14.300
Every town is on the move, swinging in the rhythm of these United States.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:23.820
Yes, in Everytown, happiness and security are challenged daily by an enemy. 

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:28.320
This enemy strikes oftenest at you. His name is tuberculosis.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:38.900
Here is a germ that causes this disease. All
of us in Everytown bear the burden of tuberculosis.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:44.700
But it weighs heaviest on those whose loved
ones it attacks and often kills. 

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.480
Tuberculosis blasts the hope of parents.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:52.740
Parents who have made uncounted sacrifices for their children. 

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.260
Tuberculosis, maker of orphans.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:00.860
[ Music ]

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:08.619
Everytown teems with industry. In the [?] home,
the enemy and his victims are easily forgotten.

00:02:08.619 --> 00:02:15.040
The youth of Everytown glory in their strength;
their zest for life. Yet tuberculosis destroys

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.620
32,000 Americans under 40 each year.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:26.620
Here is Roy. He is young. He is strong. He
is unafraid. He has heft and red blood.

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:34.020
And here, in another of Everytown's many industries
is Julie. Eager and capable.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.860
[Bell rings]

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:44.070
Yet that quitting bell has a welcome sound
when the day's work is done.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:48.480
[ Music ]

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:56.000
Life now really begins for Julie. Roy feels
the same way about his whistle blast.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:03.560
Romance begins for Julie and Roy when they
meet at the factory door.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:08.620
The old jalopy coughs and snorts, but it still goes places.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:15.630
To the rainbow for instance. A rosy rainbow
of promise.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:25.560
[ Music ]

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:31.520
The young Americans in Everytown who work hard, play hard, too. Gaiety, fun, companionship.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:37.160
These are products of normal, Everytown life.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:41.600
[ Music ]

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:46.139
Roy and Julie wouldn't miss their holiday
swim for anything. Building health and strength

00:03:46.139 --> 00:03:50.639
in the fresh air. Carefree and happy.

00:03:50.639 --> 00:03:54.099
[ Music ]

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.620
Hello? What is this? 

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.940
A hemorrhage from the lung?

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.910
[Bell ringing]

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:09.170
Everytown's health guardians are on the job
ready to serve any and all.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:13.820
Luckily for Roy, there's a first-rate sanatorium
in Everytown.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:18.910
Blood from the mouth, the physician knows,
is not to be passed up lightly. Experienced

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:22.960
Experienced hands, skilled eyes and ears, track down the cause of that hemorrhage.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:29.260
Gets the facts together. All the odds and ends of facts. 

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:35.040
Sputum and blood samples are taken, and off they go to the laboratory.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.340
[ Music ]

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:42.380
And very important, the magic eye of the x-ray.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:50.400
Only a shadow picture is produced, but the
trained eye can read what's behind those shadows

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:55.310
as clearly as you read the page of a book.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:05:01.610
The sputum sample is put through a rigid test.
The microscope aids. 

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:05.740
The germ: unmistakable.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:12.740
To the medical staff, these facts spell tuberculosis
of the left lung. Active, far advanced, 

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:14.840
and with a cavity.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:23.160
But if Roy plays the game, his chances are
good. Treatment. Absolute bed rest. 

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:28.180
And, says the Chief of Staff, "Bring this case up for review in one month."

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:31.360
Tuberculosis certainly changes Roy's life.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:35.880
It puts a sudden stop to work and play and plans for the future.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:41.220
[ Music ]

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:46.860
Rest and more rest. Rest for Roy, but not
for the case-finders.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:54.320
Every town's health workers know that each case of tuberculosis comes from some other case.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:06:00.620
Public health nurses inquire, from whom did
Roy get it? To whom has he given it?

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:03.050
Find out from his employer about his workmates.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:06.560
Is someone there who gave the disease to him?

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:10.260
Is there someone else to whom Roy may have given it?

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:18.700
This is how the germ gets from one body to
another. Now, thorough but careful detective work

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:23.020
finds out about Roy's home, his work,
his close associates.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:28.240
The nurse follows every clue. Roy's friends
are interested. 

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:35.560
Here comes a clue easy to follow. Julie, where does she live? 

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:42.880
This nurse is a contact finder. Do you remember Julie?

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:46.780
[ Music ]

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:52.860
That was lip contact. The surest way of transporting
tuberculosis germs. 

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:58.120
Don't delay, Julie. Let the doctor decide.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:04.300
Then Julie visits her physician. Besides a
routine examination of the chest, the examination

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.550
includes the tuberculin test.

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:13.550
A simple skin test which tells whether tuberculosis
germs have found a foothold in the body. 

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:18.980
Up-to-date physicians everywhere now use this test.

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:27.290
If negative, it means no tuberculosis. If
positive, it means search further.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:41.600
[ Music ]

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:46.460
Julie returns. The test is positive. 

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:50.140
The spot where the solution was injected is slightly raised and reddish.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:58.970
Julie must be x-rayed. 

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:04.100
Here are the shadows.
Expertly interpreted by her doctor, they say

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:06.600
early tuberculosis.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:13.610
Don't delay Julie, the sooner treatment is
begun, the more certain the cure.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:15.919
Bed rest now for Julie.

00:08:15.919 --> 00:08:22.260
Almost a vegetable existence it is, but reading
helps. Good reading habits help Julie, as

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:27.920
they have so many others, to readjust her life. A friendly place, the sanatorium.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:31.340
[ Music ]

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:37.220
The medical chief talks to all of the patients.
By such means, modern sanatoria educate their

00:08:37.229 --> 00:08:44.229
patients in a new way of life. Listen in with
all the patients to what the doctor says.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:51.360
Our sanatorium is but one of the many base
hospitals of a great warfare. Here we train

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:55.320
doctors, nurses, technical workers who carry
on the battle.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:09:00.360
The sanatorium is a place to care for sick
people and restore them to a useful life.

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:04.290
Here the resources of medical science are
put into practice in the treatment of the

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:07.790
patient, and the defeat of tuberculosis.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:12.110
Outside our sanatorium are other forces. Health
departments. Health workers. 

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:15.180
Educators who plan the strategy.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:23.300
The Tuberculosis Association brings the story
of tuberculosis to the public by printed matter,

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:26.680
on the picture screen, over the air.

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:33.040
Throughout the country, tuberculosis associations
backed up by the National Tuberculosis Association

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:39.820
are in every town to make war on the enemy.

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:45.130
For the physician, technical publications.
For the public, clearly written information.

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:49.460
All of this made possible by the sale of Christmas
Seals.

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:56.460
Julie listens and learns. Someday she will
become one of the soldiers fighting tuberculosis.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:10:04.230
But first comes the business of getting better,
and that means rest.

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:11.870
What news of Roy after weeks of bed rest?
The x-ray shadows tell Roy's doctor that the

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:16.130
cavity in the lung is still open. The germs
are still in his sputum. 

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:18.860
He needs special treatment.

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:24.860
The doctor arranges for Roy a simple operation
called pneumothorax.

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:26.960
A local anesthetic comes first.

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:33.420
[ Music ]

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:38.240
Very gently, air is allowed to enter between
the rigid chest wall and the soft lung tissue.

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:46.780
By means of a series of these simple operations,
the diseased lung is compressed long enough to heal.

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:52.660
Meanwhile, Roy's doctor calls a staff meeting to study Roy as a person. 

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:57.200
The librarian reports what he reads.

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:09.750
The occupational therapist explores Roy's
interests.

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:19.930
And the nurse? Roy's heart interest is no
secret to his nurse. 

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:28.700
From the state rehabilitation agent, the doctor learns more about Roy's former job.

00:11:28.709 --> 00:11:34.660
He must give this up, too. The whole trained
staff helps the doctors to understand Roy

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:41.660
and his problems. Time brings improvement.
This earns new privileges for Roy.

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:52.070
The state rehabilitation agent knows about
jobs and training for jobs. 

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:59.070
Roy's doctor calls on this knowledge to help plan a new life for Roy.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:07.100
First, Roy needs to know himself. 

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:12.200
How fast and how accurately can Roy do clerical work?

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:20.120
Does he have mechanical aptitude? How readily
does he see patterns, size, design?

00:12:25.459 --> 00:12:29.539
How well do Roy's two hands work together?

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:43.660
Has he much knack for handling small tools?

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:58.720
The answers to such questions [break in audio]
Roy a lot about himself. Now the doctor couples

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:07.900
what he knows about Roy with what the rehabilitation
agent knows of jobs and training.

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:19.010
Together they discuss various occupations.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:25.090
A final rehabilitation plan is worked out with and for Roy.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:33.820
The rehabilitation agent and Roy's former
employer work out a retraining plan in a growing industry.

00:13:38.940 --> 00:13:40.720
Roy continues to improve.

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:43.870
He earns further privileges. 

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:52.180
Ahh, what a privilege it is after months in bed, just to amble out of doors.

00:13:57.380 --> 00:14:01.880
However, leisure should not mean idleness.

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:05.900
Roy learns new forms of play more suitable to his condition. 

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:09.880
A man's hobbies may have much to do with his health.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:18.940
And then there's Julie. 

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:26.080
For what job shall
Julie be trained? Homemaking is a job too.

00:14:26.339 --> 00:14:29.760
Keeping house efficiently spares energy and
saves money.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:33.500
Julie will need her energy to keep well. 

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:41.050
A smooth-running job even in housekeeping is less tiring. Her doctor knows that well.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:46.940
So Julie is taught how to avoid hard ways
in homemaking. 

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:50.491
One can learn to work more efficiently.

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:04.520
Roy's day of graduation from the sanatorium
comes at last.

00:15:04.529 --> 00:15:08.160
[Music]

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:13.380
And it's goodbye to the sanatorium. But Roy takes with him what he has learned. 

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:21.820
Rehabilitation now goes ahead full speed.

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:25.820
[ Music ]

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:32.000
Medical checkup is not neglected. The healed
lung holds firm. 

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:39.480
Roy's training is checked by the rehabilitation agent.

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:46.480
It leads to a job. Roy has been helped to
prepare for a job he can do.

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:49.200
[Bell ringing]

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:55.360
The road back, always long and often tedious,
leads at last to happiness.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:16:04.399
[ Music ]

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:18.600
Roy and Julie. They have found the way back.
The war against tuberculosis goes on in every town.

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:23.899
Their close escape from disaster makes new
recruits of Roy and Julie. They have seen

00:16:23.899 --> 00:16:26.730
active service as casualties.

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:34.170
[ Music ]

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:40.340
They seek reenlistment with all who aid defense against tuberculosis. 

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:45.220
Their experience may help other young people to avoid disaster.

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:49.340
Their interest will last for the duration of the war.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:54.500
[ Music ]

00:16:55.720 --> 00:17:03.440
Citizens of Everytown enlist! Wipe out tuberculosis
in Everytown!

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:14.020
[ Music ]

